1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,771
Publishing a change to a versioned content item leaves the previous version in

2
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:08,667
the database, and these old versions pile up.

3
00:00:08,667 --> 00:00:11,904
Content Version Pruning deletes them on a schedule.

4
00:00:11,904 --> 00:00:16,050
In this video, we'll enable it, choose its rules, and run its task.

5
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:26,210
In a content type that is Versionable, publishing a change keeps the version it replaces.

6
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:28,493
That copy is an archived version:

7
00:00:28,493 --> 00:00:32,355
it is neither the most recent version nor the published one.

8
00:00:32,355 --> 00:00:35,750
Here, archived has nothing to do with Archive Later.

9
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:40,474
Pruning never deletes the published version or the most recent version.

10
00:00:40,474 --> 00:00:44,344
It deletes an archived version of a chosen content type only when the

11
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:48,266
version is older than the retention period and is not among the newest

12
00:00:48,266 --> 00:00:50,640
archived versions you keep for its item.

13
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:53,292
Three steps put it to work:

14
00:00:53,292 --> 00:00:58,308
enable the features, choose the rules, and enable the background task, which runs

15
00:00:58,308 --> 00:00:59,922
once a day by default.

16
00:00:59,922 --> 00:01:04,130
Pruning is permanent, because a deleted version cannot be restored.

17
00:01:08,324 --> 00:01:11,574
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for pruning.

18
00:01:11,574 --> 00:01:16,534
The Content Version Pruning feature is listed in the Content Management category.

19
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,092
Select Enable.

20
00:01:18,092 --> 00:01:22,432
The feature adds a Content Version Pruning page to the Settings menu, and

21
00:01:22,432 --> 00:01:25,563
it adds the background task that does the deleting.

22
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:29,990
The task is managed on the Background Tasks page, which has a feature

23
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:32,058
of its own in the Tasks category.

24
00:01:32,058 --> 00:01:35,185
Let's search for Background Tasks, and select Enable.

25
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:42,062
Open Settings, Content Version Pruning.

26
00:01:42,062 --> 00:01:45,056
Administrators can open this page by default.

27
00:01:45,056 --> 00:01:47,346
Other roles need two permissions:

28
00:01:47,346 --> 00:01:51,280
Manage settings, and Manage Content Version Pruning settings.

29
00:01:51,732 --> 00:01:56,227
At the top, the Disable check box stops the pruning while the feature stays enabled.

30
00:01:56,227 --> 00:02:00,173
It is separate from the switch of the background task, which comes later.

31
00:02:00,173 --> 00:02:01,622
Let's leave it cleared.

32
00:02:02,085 --> 00:02:05,145
Retention period (days) is 30 by default.

33
00:02:05,145 --> 00:02:10,745
An archived version that was last modified within this many days is not deleted.

34
00:02:11,265 --> 00:02:14,788
Archived versions to keep per item is 1 by default.

35
00:02:14,788 --> 00:02:20,844
That many of the most recent archived versions of each item always stay, whatever their age.

36
00:02:20,844 --> 00:02:23,625
A value of 0 turns this protection off.

37
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:28,744
Under Content types to prune, nothing is selected by default, and nothing is

38
00:02:28,744 --> 00:02:30,849
pruned until you select a type.

39
00:02:30,849 --> 00:02:35,003
Let's select Blog Post and Page, not Select all, so that only those

40
00:02:35,003 --> 00:02:36,539
two types are pruned.

41
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:37,989
Select Save.

42
00:02:37,989 --> 00:02:41,310
A message confirms that the site settings were updated.

43
00:02:45,556 --> 00:02:50,726
Open Tools, Background Tasks, and find the Content Version Pruning Background Task.

44
00:02:50,726 --> 00:02:54,676
Its Disabled badge shows that it does not run on its schedule.

45
00:02:55,129 --> 00:02:56,261
Select Enable.

46
00:02:56,261 --> 00:03:00,280
By default, the task then runs every day at midnight, in the time

47
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:03,620
zone of your site, and the Next run badge shows when.

48
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:07,299
Edit opens its settings, where you can change the schedule.

49
00:03:07,764 --> 00:03:11,956
To try the task before midnight, open its Actions menu and choose the

50
00:03:11,956 --> 00:03:13,856
item that runs it on demand.

51
00:03:13,856 --> 00:03:18,104
The Last run badge then shows when the task ran, and how long it took.

52
00:03:18,563 --> 00:03:23,154
On this site, there are no archived versions, so the run deletes nothing.

53
00:03:23,154 --> 00:03:27,803
On a site with older versions, each run removes the ones your rules allow.

54
00:03:29,803 --> 00:03:34,101
Content Version Pruning removes the old versions of your content on a schedule,

55
00:03:34,101 --> 00:03:35,618
by the rules you choose.

56
00:03:35,618 --> 00:03:36,933
Thanks for watching.

